<BaseLayout title="One business, however you sell." description="Kora is being built for Nigerian merchants whose orders arrive online, in chat and over the counter.">
<PageHero eyebrow="The Kora product plan" title="One business, however you sell." lede="Kora is being built for Nigerian merchants whose orders arrive online, in chat and over the counter." />
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 prose-kora">
<h2>The problem is the gap between channels</h2>
<p>The website has one stock count. WhatsApp has another order list. The shop counter has a notebook. Growing a business should not mean copying every sale between them.</p>
<h2>The product we’re building</h2>
<p>Kora puts products, inventory, orders, payments and receipts in one commerce core. A merchant dashboard, online storefront and WhatsApp assistant can then work from the same records.</p>
<h2>Starting with the foundation</h2>
<p>The first MVP focuses on variants, stock history, reservations, order handling, verified payments and branded receipts. Storefronts, official WhatsApp automation and voice ordering follow in stages. This website demonstrates that direction; it is not a live trading platform.</p>
<p><a href="/pilot" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the founding pilot</a></p>
</section>
